    "turn_text": "That's great. One of the reasons I think it's important and helpful to have veterans serving in Congress is because as you know from your service, sir, that it's, you know, in the foxhole, there's no Republican or Democrat or when you deployed, you know, your first question wasn't, you know, do you agree with me politically? It's like, are you competent? Are you well trained? Are you ready? Do you have my back in that key moment? And my sense is, having worked a little bit on the Hill, is that people with a military background tend to be more focused on getting things done a little less concerned about what part of your from.",
