    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50746.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "Without a doubt, the greatest existential threat that we face today is China and their ability to look so far into the future and prepare for the future. Their more long-term approach versus our election cycle approach of every two to four years, changing leadership and mindsets. This will, I know this isn't a political podcast, But the greatest political issue that would be on the ballot in 2020 is how serious are we about addressing the China threat. So when we look at the future of defense task force. For me, I can't speak for my co-chair, Seth Molten, but for me, it's the China threat and how we innovate and prepare the Pentagon, or really how we prepare a whole-of-government approach to tackling the China threat in a way that we haven't",
