    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "They get the China threat. And because inherently, they understand that, I take my dad, for example, my dad is retired from an automotive factory and made axles all of his life. He's seen the factory that he worked for, diminished, it's a fraction of what it used to be because of so much off-shoring to Mexico or parts coming from China. He's seen how China has wrecked the economy. But my constituents know that the American made appliances that they bought 20 years ago at whatever store they bought it from that lasted for 10 or 20 years doesn't exist anymore. But the appliances that they buy from China is broken in a year and they have to replace it. And they're paying the higher price because of the American made equipment or appliances. The company is out of business. These are intuitive issues for my constituents in northeast Indiana because they understand that China has done much to wreck our economy. But they also inherently recognize the military or national security threat too. So I don't spend a lot of time explaining or defending my almost at this point unilateral focus on China because my constituents largely get it.",
