  {
    "episode_id": 50746,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50746.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "I had the honor to interview Mac Thornberry, the senior Republican on the House Armed Service, going to May 8th, and he said it basically that exact same thing. And then Secretary McCarthy at another event said the same thing. And I would note that the Army Secretary spoke at another think tank today and reiterated many of those same points you just said, including the fact that as you may know better than me, 30 to 45 days ago, the Army ordered all of its commands to reduce their operations and maintenance expenditures by 2% because of the continuing resolution. And he explained to the listener something you understand that that has impact on training, which also impacts readiness, of course. And he also talked about how $3.5 billion in modernization funding is frozen as a result. And so he just very much underscoring what you just said.",
