    "turn_text": "who's unfortunately retiring. When he speaks in the conferences like The Voice of God, he's imminently respected by all of my colleagues, Republicans and Democrats. And he said today that a year-long CR would be a $5.6 billion cut from our deterrence efforts combating Russia and China. A lot of talk on both sides of the aisle about how important that is, but a year-long CR would hold us back from being able to contain those threats. So when he says it, people listen, but that doesn't mean that necessarily they're willing to do the right thing and come to the table. And what Mac Thornberry has taught me in three short years, this is my second year as a confere on the NDAA is that this really is all about compromise, negotiation includes maybe accepting priorities from the other side of the aisle that I might not agree with, but at the end of the day it's important to get these NDAA's passed, get them done,",
