        "text": "The House and Senate Armed Services Committees are among the last standing committees regularly passing annual authorization bills.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "It would be unfortunate if failing to pass an authorization bill became the new norm.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Failure to pass an annual authorization bill could tangibly damage national security.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a moral dimension to ensuring service members have what they need to complete missions and return safely.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Service members who swear allegiance by raising their right hand are morally deserving of full support from the nation.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "National security depends significantly on timely passage of authorization bills.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The act of raising the right hand signifies a binding commitment to serve under dangerous conditions.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "A functioning legislative process for authorizing defense spending is essential to maintaining public trust in institutions.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker’s interpretation of the situation reflects widely shared values about duty and sacrifice.",
        "confidence": 0.86
