  {
    "episode_id": 50746,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50746.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 55,
    "turn_text": "That's great. You mentioned STEM, and, you know, there was a statistic from a year or two ago that 25% of graduate students in the U.S. in STEM are Chinese nationals. Now, I'm sure the vast majority of those individuals are, you know, good intention people trying to get an education, but a small percentage, wittingly or unwittingly, are not. And so that's, as you know, where a lot of our innovation occurs. So as we're investing that innovation, if we're not careful, We're going to be enabling our adversary's ability to develop systems that they're going to use against us in future battlefields. How do we maintain our open democratic system and be welcoming to the world, maintain the best university, Indiana's home to some of our best universities, Purdue and Notre Dame. Many of those students come from foreign countries. How do we get that right? We maintain our characters are free and open society, but also protecting the innovation development that's required at our university to equip our troops.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
